{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>There is futility.</b> From the beginning of this verse until the verse \"Also this I saw, wisdom\" (Ecclesiastes 8:16) there are sixteen verses, joined in one theme. This verse too belongs to the theme above: there are righteous to whom arrives what should have arrived to the wicked — all their deeds — and the opposite. And when I saw this, I said: All is futility, whether righteous or wicked, as in the matter of \"My feet were almost turned aside, for I envied the arrogant\" (Psalms 73:2)."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:32.483246127Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}